config FREETZ_PACKAGE_DOMOTICZ_LINKY
	bool "Domoticz plugin: Linky smart meter (FR, Enedis account)"
	depends on FREETZ_PACKAGE_DOMOTICZ
	default n
	help
		consumption of a Linky (French) smart meter read from the Enedis
		web services of the distribution network operator

		It is a Python plugin of Domoticz: the package installs it into
		/usr/share/domoticz/plugins/DomoticzLinky, the directory Domoticz is
		started with (-approot of the domoticz package), and it needs no
		change of the Domoticz build.

		The plugin imports the Domoticz module and the Python standard
		library only, so no additional Python package is required.

		It reads the hourly data of an Enedis account (the same figures
		as the Enedis web site), not the teleinformation output of the
		meter: Domoticz has a native Teleinfo driver for the local
		serial/TCP reading, so the two do not overlap, and this plugin
		keeps working when the box is far from the meter or the meter has
		no local output wired to it. It needs an Enedis account and the
		public authentication proxy the plugin relies on; upstream states
		that support and updates will probably be very limited.

		Setup: Setup -> Hardware -> Linky, enter the Enedis account data.

		Licensed upstream (LICENSE is installed with the plugin). The
		repository has no release tags, so the build fetches a pinned commit of
		the default branch.
